From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Smith <scott@newtrostudios.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:57:29 -0400
Subject: remotesmith(0307): treat a silent peer as lost while it holds input

AC-41, follow-up to 0304. 0304 releases held keys and buttons when the
connection ends, but on a pulled cable the host only ends it at its
30 s receive timeout, so a held key or a drag stayed down that long.
The controller answers the host's TestDelay every second. When the
connection holds input down and the peer has missed ten heartbeats
(10 s), the host now treats the connection as lost: it ends it, and the
teardown releases everything. Shorter stalls (relay hiccups) change
nothing, so a drag or held modifier survives them; and since the session
ends rather than carrying on after a host-side release, the controller
reconnects with its real key and button state. Without held input
upstream's 30 s timeout applies unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
